From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:07:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: hardware digits on the dial screen and Recents
 privacy

Phone design (phone-dialer-titan2) on keyboards without a number row:

* Dial pad: while the number field or an on-screen key has focus, a
  hardware key that types a dial character goes through keyPressed()
  like a touch, with its DTMF tone (stopped on release): Alt+W E R S D F
  Z X C and the key map's Alt 0, plain W E R S D F Z X C, the number
  row, numpad, *, # and +. A held key types once. Shift+letter and
  Ctrl/Meta/Fn chords keep their upstream meaning. Pure policy:
  sable/SableDialpadKeys.java.
* Main screen: with the dial pad closed and no text field focused, a
  digit from the Alt layer, number row or numpad opens the dial pad with
  that digit through the same ACTION_DIAL path other apps use. Plain
  letters are untouched.
* Recents privacy: while the device is locked or Sable private mode is
  on (Sable Hub > Connected apps; read from Hub's read-only
  org.sableos.hub.privacy provider off the main thread on resume), rows
  show the call type, date and "Contact hidden": no name, number,
  location, account line or photo, and the accessibility text says the
  same. Calling back is unchanged and the call log is never written.
  Without Hub there is no private mode.

Telephony, emergency calling and the in-call screen are untouched.
